('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct preposition: I agree ___ your suggestion.','[{"id":"A","text":"to"},{"id":"B","text":"for"},{"id":"C","text":"from"},{"id":"D","text":"with"}]'::jsonb,'D','The standard combination is agree with.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct preposition: She listens ___ the radio.','[{"id":"A","text":"for"},{"id":"B","text":"with"},{"id":"C","text":"to"},{"id":"D","text":"at"}]'::jsonb,'C','The standard verb-preposition combination is listen to.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct preposition: They are waiting ___ the bus.','[{"id":"A","text":"of"},{"id":"B","text":"for"},{"id":"C","text":"to"},{"id":"D","text":"with"}]'::jsonb,'B','The standard combination is wait for.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct pronoun: The teacher spoke to Ada and ___.','[{"id":"A","text":"I"},{"id":"B","text":"we"},{"id":"C","text":"they"},{"id":"D","text":"me"}]'::jsonb,'D','The pronoun is the object of the preposition to, so objective case me is correct.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct sentence about one item.','[{"id":"A","text":"One of the books were missing now."},{"id":"B","text":"One of the books is missing."},{"id":"C","text":"One of the books are missing."},{"id":"D","text":"One of the books be missing."}]'::jsonb,'B','The head subject one is singular, so is agrees with it.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct sentence for a plural subject.','[{"id":"A","text":"The students am ready."},{"id":"B","text":"The students be ready."},{"id":"C","text":"The students are ready."},{"id":"D","text":"The students is ready."}]'::jsonb,'C','The plural subject students agrees with are.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct sentence.','[{"id":"A","text":"She have finished her work."},{"id":"B","text":"She has finish her work."},{"id":"C","text":"She finishing has her work."},{"id":"D","text":"She has finished her work."}]'::jsonb,'D','The present perfect uses has/have plus the past participle.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Choose the correct subject-verb agreement.','[{"id":"A","text":"The boy plays football."},{"id":"B","text":"The boy play football."},{"id":"C","text":"The boys plays football."},{"id":"D","text":"The boy playing football."}]'::jsonb,'A','A singular third-person subject takes plays in the simple present.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which form is a present perfect question?','[{"id":"A","text":"Do you have finished?"},{"id":"B","text":"Are you finish?"},{"id":"C","text":"Have you finished?"},{"id":"D","text":"Did you finished?"}]'::jsonb,'C','Present perfect questions use have/has plus the past participle.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which phrase correctly uses for to express duration?','[{"id":"A","text":"for yesterday"},{"id":"B","text":"for three years"},{"id":"C","text":"for 2020"},{"id":"D","text":"for last Monday"}]'::jsonb,'B','For is used for a period or duration.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which phrase correctly uses since?','[{"id":"A","text":"since two hours"},{"id":"B","text":"since several months"},{"id":"C","text":"since 2020"},{"id":"D","text":"since three years"}]'::jsonb,'C','Since refers to a point in time.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which pronoun is in the possessive case?','[{"id":"A","text":"theirs"},{"id":"B","text":"them"},{"id":"C","text":"they"},{"id":"D","text":"who"}]'::jsonb,'A','Theirs expresses possession.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which sentence correctly uses the present perfect?','[{"id":"A","text":"I live here since 2021."},{"id":"B","text":"I am living here since 2021."},{"id":"C","text":"I lived here since 2021 and still do."},{"id":"D","text":"I have lived here since 2021."}]'::jsonb,'D','Present perfect is used for a situation that began in the past and continues to the present.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which sentence uses yet naturally with the present perfect?','[{"id":"A","text":"I have finish yesterday."},{"id":"B","text":"I haven''t finished yet."},{"id":"C","text":"I didn''t finished yet."},{"id":"D","text":"I am not finish yet."}]'::jsonb,'B','Yet commonly appears in present-perfect negatives and questions.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','157498ec-9692-44b7-a733-02b697336f85'::uuid,'Grammar & Structure','Which tense is most suitable for a completed action at a definite past time such as yesterday?','[{"id":"A","text":"Past simple"},{"id":"B","text":"Present perfect"},{"id":"C","text":"Future perfect"},{"id":"D","text":"Present continuous"}]'::jsonb,'A','Past simple is normally used for a definite completed past time.','medium','Cambridge / British Council / Purdue grammar references','https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/present-perfect-simple-i-','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','A fake website designed to imitate a trusted login page is commonly used in:','[{"id":"A","text":"Spreadsheet formatting"},{"id":"B","text":"Image rendering"},{"id":"C","text":"Phishing"},{"id":"D","text":"Defragmentation"}]'::jsonb,'C','Phishing often uses fake websites that imitate trusted services.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','A second authentication factor is valuable because it:','[{"id":"A","text":"Disables account security"},{"id":"B","text":"Adds another proof of identity"},{"id":"C","text":"Makes every password public"},{"id":"D","text":"Removes the need for identity checks"}]'::jsonb,'B','A second factor adds another layer of identity verification.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','If an attacker obtains an offline copy of password hashes, why is password strength important?','[{"id":"A","text":"The account changes owner automatically"},{"id":"B","text":"The keyboard is disabled"},{"id":"C","text":"Attackers can make many guesses without normal login-page limits"},{"id":"D","text":"The monitor becomes damaged"}]'::jsonb,'C','Offline guessing can allow very large numbers of password guesses.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','What is phishing?','[{"id":"A","text":"A database backup process"},{"id":"B","text":"A trick that attempts to make a user reveal credentials or sensitive information"},{"id":"C","text":"A method of compressing files"},{"id":"D","text":"A type of printer"}]'::jsonb,'B','NIST describes phishing as tricking users into giving away credentials or information.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','What is the main purpose of authentication?','[{"id":"A","text":"To verify identity before granting access"},{"id":"B","text":"To increase screen resolution"},{"id":"C","text":"To compress documents"},{"id":"D","text":"To sort files alphabetically"}]'::jsonb,'A','Authentication verifies a user''s identity before access is granted.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Which action is safest after receiving a suspicious login link?','[{"id":"A","text":"Avoid entering credentials and verify the site independently"},{"id":"B","text":"Enter the password quickly"},{"id":"C","text":"Forward your password to the sender"},{"id":"D","text":"Disable browser security warnings"}]'::jsonb,'A','Suspicious links can be phishing attempts; credentials should not be entered without verification.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Which attack relies heavily on social engineering to steal passwords?','[{"id":"A","text":"File indexing"},{"id":"B","text":"Data sorting"},{"id":"C","text":"Disk partitioning"},{"id":"D","text":"Phishing"}]'::jsonb,'D','Phishing is a common social-engineering route for credential theft.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Which credential choice is especially poor security practice?','[{"id":"A","text":"Using a unique password"},{"id":"B","text":"Using multifactor authentication"},{"id":"C","text":"Checking a site address"},{"id":"D","text":"Using 12345 as a password"}]'::jsonb,'D','NIST highlights common passwords such as 12345 as weak choices.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Which practice is safer for separate online accounts?','[{"id":"A","text":"Turn off all authentication"},{"id":"B","text":"Use unique passwords"},{"id":"C","text":"Use the same short password"},{"id":"D","text":"Publish passwords in notes online"}]'::jsonb,'B','Unique passwords limit the damage from credential compromise.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Which step improves account security beyond relying only on a password?','[{"id":"A","text":"Using multifactor authentication"},{"id":"B","text":"Reusing the same password everywhere"},{"id":"C","text":"Sharing passwords with friends"},{"id":"D","text":"Disabling login alerts"}]'::jsonb,'A','NIST recommends stronger authentication such as multifactor authentication.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Why can very simple passwords be unsafe?','[{"id":"A","text":"They prevent internet access"},{"id":"B","text":"They encrypt files automatically"},{"id":"C","text":"They may be easy for attackers to guess"},{"id":"D","text":"They always damage hardware"}]'::jsonb,'C','NIST warns that common passwords are easy for attackers to guess.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','22f09930-c43f-4b8b-bec2-a2fa667b7a99'::uuid,'Cybersecurity','Why is reusing the same password on many sites risky?','[{"id":"A","text":"It makes monitors brighter"},{"id":"B","text":"It slows internet speed"},{"id":"C","text":"It changes file formats"},{"id":"D","text":"A breach on one site can threaten other accounts using the same password"}]'::jsonb,'D','Password reuse can let one breached credential compromise multiple accounts.','medium','NIST Cybersecurity and Privacy','https://www.nist.gov/cybersecurity-and-privacy/how-do-i-create-good-password','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','A vehicle used to operate a business and not held for sale is normally what type of asset?','[{"id":"A","text":"Noncurrent/fixed asset"},{"id":"B","text":"Current liability"},{"id":"C","text":"Revenue item"},{"id":"D","text":"Dividend"}]'::jsonb,'A','Operational vehicles are generally fixed/noncurrent assets.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','After liabilities are deducted from assets, the remaining owners'' interest is called what?','[{"id":"A","text":"Revenue"},{"id":"B","text":"Inventory"},{"id":"C","text":"Gross sales"},{"id":"D","text":"Equity"}]'::jsonb,'D','Equity is the residual interest after liabilities.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','For a business, cash is generally classified as what?','[{"id":"A","text":"A dividend"},{"id":"B","text":"An asset"},{"id":"C","text":"A liability"},{"id":"D","text":"An expense only"}]'::jsonb,'B','Cash is an asset.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','For a trading business, unsold inventory is normally classified as what?','[{"id":"A","text":"A tax"},{"id":"B","text":"An asset"},{"id":"C","text":"A liability"},{"id":"D","text":"A dividend"}]'::jsonb,'B','Inventory is an asset.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','In business finance, which equation must a balance sheet satisfy?','[{"id":"A","text":"Liabilities = Cash + Sales"},{"id":"B","text":"Assets = Liabilities + Shareholders'' Equity"},{"id":"C","text":"Revenue = Assets + Cash"},{"id":"D","text":"Assets = Revenue - Expenses"}]'::jsonb,'B','A balance sheet follows Assets = Liabilities + Shareholders'' Equity.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','Money a business owes to a supplier is generally classified as what?','[{"id":"A","text":"A liability"},{"id":"B","text":"An asset"},{"id":"C","text":"A dividend"},{"id":"D","text":"Revenue"}]'::jsonb,'A','Amounts owed to suppliers are liabilities.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','Which classification normally applies to an asset expected to turn into cash within a year?','[{"id":"A","text":"Equity reserve"},{"id":"B","text":"Revenue"},{"id":"C","text":"Current asset"},{"id":"D","text":"Long-term liability"}]'::jsonb,'C','Such an item is generally a current asset.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','Which statement focuses on cash moving into and out of a company?','[{"id":"A","text":"Sales invoice"},{"id":"B","text":"Share certificate"},{"id":"C","text":"Cash flow statement"},{"id":"D","text":"Balance sheet only"}]'::jsonb,'C','The cash flow statement reports cash inflows and outflows.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','Which statement is most useful for reviewing revenue and expenses over a period?','[{"id":"A","text":"Balance sheet"},{"id":"B","text":"Share certificate"},{"id":"C","text":"Purchase order"},{"id":"D","text":"Income statement"}]'::jsonb,'D','An income statement reports revenues and expenses over a period.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','32929c31-b38c-4e52-8214-b656cca924b0'::uuid,'Business Finance','Which statement is used to view a company''s financial position at one date?','[{"id":"A","text":"Balance sheet"},{"id":"B","text":"Income statement"},{"id":"C","text":"Cash flow statement"},{"id":"D","text":"Sales invoice"}]'::jsonb,'A','A balance sheet shows financial position at a point in time.','medium','U.S. SEC Beginner''s Guide to Financial Statements','https://www.sec.gov/files/investor/pubs/begfinstmtguide.htm','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Genetics & Heredity','How many pairs of chromosomes are normally found in a human somatic cell nucleus?','[{"id":"A","text":"22"},{"id":"B","text":"44"},{"id":"C","text":"46"},{"id":"D","text":"23"}]'::jsonb,'D','Human somatic cells normally contain 23 chromosome pairs.','medium','NHGRI genome education','https://www.genome.gov/25520226/online-education-kit-transcript-exploring-our-molecular-selves','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Genetics & Heredity','In DNA, adenine most commonly pairs with which base?','[{"id":"A","text":"Guanine"},{"id":"B","text":"Uracil"},{"id":"C","text":"Thymine"},{"id":"D","text":"Cytosine"}]'::jsonb,'C','In DNA base pairing, adenine pairs with thymine.','medium','NHGRI genome education','https://www.genome.gov/25520226/online-education-kit-transcript-exploring-our-molecular-selves','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Genetics & Heredity','In DNA, cytosine most commonly pairs with which base?','[{"id":"A","text":"Uracil"},{"id":"B","text":"Guanine"},{"id":"C","text":"Thymine"},{"id":"D","text":"Adenine"}]'::jsonb,'B','In DNA base pairing, cytosine pairs with guanine.','medium','NHGRI genome education','https://www.genome.gov/25520226/online-education-kit-transcript-exploring-our-molecular-selves','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Plant Biology','In eukaryotic plant cells, photosynthesis occurs mainly in which organelle?','[{"id":"A","text":"Chloroplast"},{"id":"B","text":"Mitochondrion"},{"id":"C","text":"Nucleus"},{"id":"D","text":"Ribosome"}]'::jsonb,'A','Photosynthesis occurs in chloroplasts.','medium','NIH/NCBI biology reference','https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK9861/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Plant Biology','The light reactions of photosynthesis occur mainly in the:','[{"id":"A","text":"Nuclear envelope"},{"id":"B","text":"Cell wall"},{"id":"C","text":"Cytosol"},{"id":"D","text":"Thylakoid membrane"}]'::jsonb,'D','The light reactions occur in the thylakoid membrane.','medium','NIH/NCBI biology reference','https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK9861/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Plant Biology','The reactions that synthesize glucose in photosynthesis occur mainly in the chloroplast:','[{"id":"A","text":"Outer membrane"},{"id":"B","text":"Cell wall"},{"id":"C","text":"Stroma"},{"id":"D","text":"Thylakoid lumen"}]'::jsonb,'C','Glucose-synthesizing reactions occur in the stroma.','medium','NIH/NCBI biology reference','https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK9861/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Plant Biology','Which gas is formed from water during the light reactions of photosynthesis?','[{"id":"A","text":"Methane"},{"id":"B","text":"Oxygen"},{"id":"C","text":"Nitrogen"},{"id":"D","text":"Carbon dioxide"}]'::jsonb,'B','The light reactions are coupled to formation of oxygen from water.','medium','NIH/NCBI biology reference','https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK9861/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Genetics & Heredity','Which molecule carries genetic information in chromosomes?','[{"id":"A","text":"DNA"},{"id":"B","text":"ATP"},{"id":"C","text":"Glucose"},{"id":"D","text":"Cholesterol"}]'::jsonb,'A','Chromosomes contain long molecules of DNA.','medium','NHGRI genome education','https://www.genome.gov/25520226/online-education-kit-transcript-exploring-our-molecular-selves','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Genetics & Heredity','Which molecule is produced when RNA polymerase copies information from a gene?','[{"id":"A","text":"Glycogen"},{"id":"B","text":"ATP only"},{"id":"C","text":"Cellulose"},{"id":"D","text":"Messenger RNA"}]'::jsonb,'D','RNA polymerase copies gene information into messenger RNA.','medium','NHGRI genome education','https://www.genome.gov/25520226/online-education-kit-transcript-exploring-our-molecular-selves','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Cell Biology','Which organelle contains its own DNA in eukaryotic cells?','[{"id":"A","text":"Lysosome"},{"id":"B","text":"Mitochondrion"},{"id":"C","text":"Golgi apparatus"},{"id":"D","text":"Smooth endoplasmic reticulum"}]'::jsonb,'B','Mitochondria contain their own DNA.','medium','NIH/NCBI biology reference','https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK9896/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Cell Biology','Which organelle is especially important for ATP production by oxidative phosphorylation in eukaryotic cells?','[{"id":"A","text":"Lysosome"},{"id":"B","text":"Nucleolus"},{"id":"C","text":"Mitochondrion"},{"id":"D","text":"Golgi apparatus"}]'::jsonb,'C','Mitochondria generate much of the cell''s ATP through oxidative phosphorylation.','medium','NIH/NCBI biology reference','https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK9896/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Genetics & Heredity','Which statement correctly explains the concept tested by this prompt: "How many pairs of chromosomes are normally found in a human somatic cell nucleus"?','[{"id":"A","text":"The concept is unrelated to cellular or hereditary processes."},{"id":"B","text":"The opposite of the verified biological relationship is always true."},{"id":"C","text":"The process occurs only outside living organisms."},{"id":"D","text":"Human somatic cells normally contain 23 chromosome pairs."}]'::jsonb,'D','Human somatic cells normally contain 23 chromosome pairs.','hard','NHGRI genome education','https://www.genome.gov/25520226/online-education-kit-transcript-exploring-our-molecular-selves','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Genetics & Heredity','Which statement correctly explains the concept tested by this prompt: "In DNA, adenine most commonly pairs with which base"?','[{"id":"A","text":"The opposite of the verified biological relationship is always true."},{"id":"B","text":"The process occurs only outside living organisms."},{"id":"C","text":"In DNA base pairing, adenine pairs with thymine."},{"id":"D","text":"The concept is unrelated to cellular or hereditary processes."}]'::jsonb,'C','In DNA base pairing, adenine pairs with thymine.','hard','NHGRI genome education','https://www.genome.gov/25520226/online-education-kit-transcript-exploring-our-molecular-selves','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Genetics & Heredity','Which statement correctly explains the concept tested by this prompt: "In DNA, cytosine most commonly pairs with which base"?','[{"id":"A","text":"The process occurs only outside living organisms."},{"id":"B","text":"In DNA base pairing, cytosine pairs with guanine."},{"id":"C","text":"The concept is unrelated to cellular or hereditary processes."},{"id":"D","text":"The opposite of the verified biological relationship is always true."}]'::jsonb,'B','In DNA base pairing, cytosine pairs with guanine.','hard','NHGRI genome education','https://www.genome.gov/25520226/online-education-kit-transcript-exploring-our-molecular-selves','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Plant Biology','Which statement correctly explains the concept tested by this prompt: "In eukaryotic plant cells, photosynthesis occurs mainly in which organelle"?','[{"id":"A","text":"Photosynthesis occurs in chloroplasts."},{"id":"B","text":"The concept is unrelated to cellular or hereditary processes."},{"id":"C","text":"The opposite of the verified biological relationship is always true."},{"id":"D","text":"The process occurs only outside living organisms."}]'::jsonb,'A','Photosynthesis occurs in chloroplasts.','hard','NIH/NCBI biology reference','https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK9861/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Plant Biology','Which statement correctly explains the concept tested by this prompt: "The light reactions of photosynthesis occur mainly in the:"?','[{"id":"A","text":"The concept is unrelated to cellular or hereditary processes."},{"id":"B","text":"The opposite of the verified biological relationship is always true."},{"id":"C","text":"The process occurs only outside living organisms."},{"id":"D","text":"The light reactions occur in the thylakoid membrane."}]'::jsonb,'D','The light reactions occur in the thylakoid membrane.','hard','NIH/NCBI biology reference','https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK9861/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Plant Biology','Which statement correctly explains the concept tested by this prompt: "The reactions that synthesize glucose in photosynthesis occur mainly in the chloroplast:"?','[{"id":"A","text":"The opposite of the verified biological relationship is always true."},{"id":"B","text":"The process occurs only outside living organisms."},{"id":"C","text":"Glucose-synthesizing reactions occur in the stroma."},{"id":"D","text":"The concept is unrelated to cellular or hereditary processes."}]'::jsonb,'C','Glucose-synthesizing reactions occur in the stroma.','hard','NIH/NCBI biology reference','https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK9861/','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Genetics & Heredity','Which statement correctly explains the concept tested by this prompt: "Which molecule carries genetic information in chromosomes"?','[{"id":"A","text":"Chromosomes contain long molecules of DNA."},{"id":"B","text":"The concept is unrelated to cellular or hereditary processes."},{"id":"C","text":"The opposite of the verified biological relationship is always true."},{"id":"D","text":"The process occurs only outside living organisms."}]'::jsonb,'A','Chromosomes contain long molecules of DNA.','hard','NHGRI genome education','https://www.genome.gov/25520226/online-education-kit-transcript-exploring-our-molecular-selves','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
('waec','5f347f7d-3a09-46b9-9275-6a5c9ca12470'::uuid,'Genetics & Heredity','Which statement correctly explains the concept tested by this prompt: "Which molecule is produced when RNA polymerase copies information from a gene"?','[{"id":"A","text":"The concept is unrelated to cellular or hereditary processes."},{"id":"B","text":"The opposite of the verified biological relationship is always true."},{"id":"C","text":"The process occurs only outside living organisms."},{"id":"D","text":"RNA polymerase copies gene information into messenger RNA."}]'::jsonb,'D','RNA polymerase copies gene information into messenger RNA.','hard','NHGRI genome education','https://www.genome.gov/25520226/online-education-kit-transcript-exploring-our-molecular-selves','authoritative-web',now(),true,now()),
